name{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334772/selection/ma-v1/c006e3b2d62d51288b5a8ccf76eb6c455f2424789bec998746ea193b08fed605"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334766/selection/f2fe2e12cc87499aedd88cc966746cc4ec463eff610816a6e0e2a3eb3e97fcf7" :answer/id #uuid "9bb41879-462a-528e-8dbd-4364eadb1d87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\b