ed}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335271/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335271"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335262/field-1/2d5514a6a2c5e2f24d3f77c2dd21712a121dbbba853a0b47a5dda9b74f2a6eb2" :answer/id #uuid "298bd6f2-32b2-50a3-9fca-6f3d5380ae2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cos(7t)-3\\sin(7t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335262/field-1/e24d3bb27515f84684be0baad1aba17ae8b1517ddee78ee5a72730c85a0c061b" :answer/id #uuid "d6eddcc9-5d04-5ea2-b57d-abe4db9609f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cos(7t)+3\\sin(7t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335262/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea89e8e6-c71a-5c5b-8fb1-