gin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333971/field-1" "q-333971/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333971"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-335267"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection/eb0bc9897bd55872a18326f7854ff7c47b8e79603ab84604507072e307e8d455" :answer/id #uuid "bd1a0761-a749-5ca4-ad21-ca6f377899cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection/d244610fc0a718e6789955eb032c705537e51ac06754fe258089419f70551c25" :answer/id #uuid "74687206-c506-56eb-beef-0d93774c24fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection/62abbf4fa8127926ef1657c61c31d78db5f3912eb52a3f138b36a09d09fba211" :answer/id #uuid "0c324707-3a02-5f25-9695-787ab1f2de99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection/8b5986ceed34057fd1a31a4ad6c05695c17a877a9ba6d8067819510db6021bcd" :answer/id #uuid "321c4cd9-1766-5a0a-aa57-0b4c7e7a8c77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection/b9e30c24ebbfc1bbb6143904a8fc808f3e68aa4e674029fc33a65408d6f16b4a" :answer/id #uuid "685df301-118e-5a58-bf75-9477e2eb66fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d57a8587-73bc-5db1-84f4-9abe5e0d13c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-335451/selection/eb0bc9897bd55872a18326f7854ff7c47b8e79603ab84604507072e307e8d455" :answer-field/choices ["q-335451/selection/eb0bc9897bd55872a18326f7854ff7c47b8e79603ab84604507072e307e8d455" "q-335451/selection/d244610fc0a718e6789955eb032c705537e51ac06754fe258089419f70551c25" "q-335451/selection/62abbf4fa8127926ef1657c61c31d78db5f3912eb52a3f138b36a09d09fba211" "q-335451/selection/8b5986ceed34057fd1a31a4ad6c05695c17a877a9ba6d8067819510db6021bcd" "q-335451/selection/b9e30c24ebbfc1bbb6143904a8fc808f3e68aa4e674029fc33a65408d6f16b4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335451" :question/id #uuid "f9955beb-b280-5cd1-9ad5-1f967a36652c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335451" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-2) \\\\ y(-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have \n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-(-2))}\\,x(-2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335451/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335451"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335448/selection/2c2a65a87bffd8ae77995f84675d