caa50629f7094042a75e0bb2218f155cf77e8976acde4635a4" "q-335448/selection/664391b57be87f28c69d845deb52d378ac92ac9561e74c079924cdfe7e23b75a" "q-335448/selection/4beec052da64d53f8010a3674d9f6122ab936a74efb2739dd95360d920bd22d7" "q-335448/selection/df66b73cbf0ef11a1d2573334275ad65ec6444f9f844cda22c5c29370c342528"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335448" :question/id #uuid "6ab60b60-d1a6-5ef2-aaf8-6579001f22b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335448" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335448/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335448"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335430/field-1/d5fd57bfc8c1c99dd4431ce65c4bce6e22c4a2d9aff789a8362b20422891ca71" :answer/id #uuid "977fb858-e00b-57cb-92fe-34346220f444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(t+3)e^{7(t+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335430/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ec36eb-3c0c-5793-8fc9-050c3a67e5b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335430/field-1/d5fd57bfc8c1c99dd4431ce65c4bce6e22c4a2d9aff789a8362b20422891ca71" :answer-field/choices ["q-335430/field-1/d5fd57bfc8c1c99dd4431ce65c4bce6e22c4a2d9aff789a8362b20422891ca71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335430/field-2/133b10d41d8ff1655629beb62b5932819cb02ce398184b21b20595cf32466895" :answer/id #uuid "ef5fd92b-617a-562e-9fe8-338338f28723" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{7(t+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335430/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f100bad-4b05-59d1-80d4-2cbc7cf84e38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335430/field-2/133b10d41d8ff1655629beb62b5932819cb02ce398184b21b20595cf32466895" :answer-field/choices ["q-335430/field-2/133b10d41d8ff1655629beb62b5932819cb02ce398184b21b20595cf32466895"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335430" :question/id #uuid "77e4d91e-a2e3-5146-a546-2cdc835ec908" :question/math-academy-id "q-335430" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-3) \\\\ y(-3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+3)}\\,x(-3) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7(t+3)} & (t+3){e}^{7(t+3)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7(t+3)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(-2t-6){e}^{7(t+3)}\\, \\\\ \\,-2{e}^{7(t+3)}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335430/field-1" "q-335430/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335430"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273/field-1/124689bb7063bd37c26e60b92e7d11bc2869aa0142ebc0a9dca9694d094571ab" :answer/id #uuid "b6636fd0-4749-59a4-8b76-eef9487641a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(t-2)e^{3(t-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273/field-1/863285b3c562573d9738217a071bcd7354b5bdd3eeeccf5400b0d9b21bca1b70" :answer/id #uuid "728c5e71-5fd1-5a98-9201-adf7dcefe959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-(t-2)e^{3(t-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ff0f9d-dfdf-51f9-910c-18814c34489b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335273/field-1/124689bb7063bd37c26e60b92e7d11bc2869aa0142ebc0a9dca9694d094571ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-335273/field-1/124689bb7063bd37c26e60b92e7d11bc2869aa0142ebc0a9dca9694d094571ab" "q-335273/field-1/863285b3c562573d9738217a071bcd7354b5bdd3eeeccf5400b0d9b21bca1b70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273/field-2/ef4310b6ecdf9f0cf2b50db7ad2dad160af71c217a67bc934485b6709699270e" :answer/id #uuid "6b6acca2-147b-5ca6-836a-a53266e20971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{3(t-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf476015-40d3-556b-9e37-8bcdbbec4844" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335273/field-2/ef4310b6ecdf9f0cf2b50db7ad2dad160af71c217a67bc934485b6709699270e" :answer-field/choices ["q-335273/field-2/ef4310b6ecdf9f0cf2b50db7ad2dad160af71c217a67bc934485b6709699270e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335273" :question/id #uuid "57c282b6-8400-51d9-92b2-8331bb08e0f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335273" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-2)} & (t-2){e}^{3(t-2)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-2)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}\\, \\\\ \\,{e}^{3(t-2)}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335273/field-1" "q-335273/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335273"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335429/field-1/1885e9c3786a150144f128d2dcd3d843ebb210985bcba83f66fbeee2a1e969f7" :answer/id #uuid "03876557-bbe0-5e1c-b14e-d3042579aa8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5-t)e^{t-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335429/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad556fc7-cbfe-5afd-bca7-1d723006dc93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335429/field-1/1885e9c3786a150144f128d2dcd3d843ebb210985bcba83f66fbeee2a1e969f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-335429/field-1/1885e9c3786a150144f128d2dcd3d843ebb210985bcba83f66fbeee2a1e969f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335429/field-2/faf860fe7bd9702ea855b9d2cdc33ea37819c6f1faf1a5ac3f43ca5f3d722404" :answer/id #uuid "fcc2641f-a40e-5c96-a53e-7b50fd7d5061" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-e^{t-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335429/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e15cc9a0-eab4-5c60-bdc7-1148bec9fcdc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335429/field-2/faf860fe7bd9702ea855b9d2cdc33ea37819c6f1faf1a5ac3f43ca5f3d722404" :answer-field/choices ["q-335429/field-2/faf860fe7bd9702ea855b9d2cdc33ea37819c6f1faf1a5ac3f43ca5f3d722404"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335429" :question/id #uuid "821b31cc-7595-5d0f-9fc7-1742bffe7ae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-335429" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(4) \\\\ y(4)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & t{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-4)}\\,x(4) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t-4} & (t-4){e}^{t-4} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t-4}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,(5-t){e}^{t-4}\\, \\\\ \\,-{e}^{t-4}\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335429/field-1" "q-335429/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-1/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" :answer/id #uuid "9756b0dd-50d5-50ec-800e-ae163a7c5e97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-1/e3a6cb9e213c821a3331fe56ca04bc11dcb8155e9f4846775e85149d35b3cb76" :answer/id #uuid "f7f841a8-4b9f-55fd-a4a4-049ed0ac219b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "by substitution from line $\\text{L2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-1/86cc1658e625ae810e72e8acf1042be3e1f61749b982ae7ff104797635ee0737" :answer/id #uuid "92090a3f-e600-57db-b239-e88a332ffad8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using the fact that ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "475fcb80-1424-5462-a360-cae20cbfd378" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337109/field-1/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-337109/field-1/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" "q-337109/field-1/e3a6cb9e213c821a3331fe56ca04bc11dcb8155e9f4846775e85149d35b3cb76" "q-337109/field-1/86cc1658e625ae810e72e8acf1042be3e1f61749b982ae7ff104797635ee0737"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-2/ec492fb997e3afd0d7bc3be56c2489fbe121747f459e8478e0349a3fa01939e8" :answer/id #uuid "2546ee97-a118-5674-9254-d2ac0fa15704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A{t}_{0}}I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-2/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02" :answer/id #uuid "d3733ef8-0386-5380-aa6f-923f1db46b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-2/175c061f136a442ead0b94a6c0974d0f9f0863371621fd38a66dce770c7a4278" :answer/id #uuid "bc0fa361-feb4-5a28-b378-30b69e163521" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa7f4509-2b5d-53c8-ad4d-5b60174cc47b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337109/field-2/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02" :answer-field/choices ["q-337109/field-2/ec492fb997e3afd0d7bc3be56c2489fbe121747f459e8478e0349a3fa01939e8" "q-337109/field-2/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02" "q-337109/field-2/175c061f136a442ead0b94a6c0974d0f9f0863371621fd38a66dce770c7a4278"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-3/79638d6522d421e35b443bd30078efa4d335aed6564d54b80ab4cd9409378f7e" :answer/id #uuid "62a444b8-bd0b-5620-aaca-bb2aa8358b68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-3/bdcc209ada28288d6eb8133014ef9a8b516df1c1e43b86db917cf5179ff24132" :answer/id #uuid "36c9a3e7-719c-5080-ba8f-85cfe108f4c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At}$ for any matrix $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-3/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595" :answer/id #uuid "b7448189-80c0-5cbe-983e-e3e36d61b5ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "11d9f67e-ce9e-571d-a3c7-274139a63ca9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337109/field-3/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595" :answer-field/choices ["q-337109/field-3/79638d6522d421e35b443bd30078efa4d335aed6564d54b80ab4cd9409378f7e" "q-337109/field-3/bdcc209ada28288d6eb8133014ef9a8b516df1c1e43b86db917cf5179ff24132" "q-337109/field-3/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337109" :question/id #uuid "5c06019e-492b-58e8-b441-055a14820869" :question/math-academy-id "q-337109" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$  Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337109/field-1" "q-337109/field-2" "q-337109/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-1/6d13565983430061aebcc723c56cc968f3fcce83a1e8672d49b43ca59d5fe3f7" :answer/id #uuid "4c24a775-a2ea-5869-989e-08449ae4d3ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating $x(t)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-1/9c44f6ff1665974fde2325d40fc833f804243b40a7ad727bd14c4ce9ae636783" :answer/id #uuid "b866f10c-468e-5891-ab43-7f8357cc8b01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using the identity $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-1/e444da7d0ecdb156dd62382b0fac142cab117caeaa0559ba07700c5f581b15ed" :answer/id #uuid "e52d0878-989b-508d-a171-20e42a5f12ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb5f316-9ea3-5d32-836d-27026f9f73b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337121/field-1/e444da7d0ecdb156dd62382b0fac142cab117caeaa0559ba07700c5f581b15ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-337121/field-1/6d13565983430061aebcc723c56cc968f3fcce83a1e8672d49b43ca59d5fe3f7" "q-337121/field-1/9c44f6ff1665974fde2325d40fc833f804243b40a7ad727bd14c4ce9ae636783" "q-337121/field-1/e444da7d0ecdb156dd62382b0fac142cab117caeaa0559ba07700c5f581b15ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-2/3aa6f3d85394d9e48304ff8e0ca20dc68533c9cc8fabc9853fd3423b253f219a" :answer/id #uuid "4362c7dd-9819-5ee1-9b93-ffc687d79b84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-2/2603f7f895b6deed8da7fc08eb5c46068c0113343e7756682b8cf713843be83a" :answer/id #uuid "8580eeb0-31c1-5321-a470-1484bf5e35ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t={t}_{0}$ and solving for $c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b" :answer/id #uuid "4e2ad203-123c-5a5c-af72-d2cf01a4a648" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b084338-c9a9-5a26-861a-23704e59f3c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337121/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b" :answer-field/choices ["q-337121/field-2/3aa6f3d85394d9e48304ff8e0ca20dc68533c9cc8fabc9853fd3423b253f219a" "q-337121/field-2/2603f7f895b6deed8da7fc08eb5c46068c0113343e7756682b8cf713843be83a" "q-337121/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-3/7e2e21aa536ea80cbf601a405abd3f3cc2f8b4ea39b9ced040dd5f4e688f4ef3" :answer/id #uuid "06183b45-ac1c-5fce-8393-a758ef0b65a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-3/4c92a695a061757d4b46494aab7d73a415e4c9ec5c6f711db04fa937a94b87ea" :answer/id #uuid "c1c99914-a0b3-5e4e-9e29-b2606def1c06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the identity ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{XY}$ for matrices" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-3/718e97f7cd4eb7c704f095d8f0eccf5ae1dba5552deb8a2b4a155f89697d0327" :answer/id #uuid "8333686f-b287-5b6c-99c1-b00bcb66fa6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "574fb82f-0a72-58d8-aff3-dcff2c4ecee6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337121/field-3/718e97f7cd4eb7c704f095d8f0eccf5ae1dba5552deb8a2b4a155f89697d0327" :answer-field/choices ["q-337121/field-3/7e2e21aa536ea80cbf601a405abd3f3cc2f8b4ea39b9ced040dd5f4e688f4ef3" "q-337121/field-3/4c92a695a061757d4b46494aab7d73a415e4c9ec5c6f711db04fa937a94b87ea" "q-337121/field-3/718e97f7cd4eb7c704f095d8f0eccf5ae1dba5552deb8a2b4a155f89697d0327"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337121" :question/id #uuid "0d9118b1-b0ff-5db4-a05c-ec3ad938a6f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337121" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Starting from $\\text{L4},$\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides on the left by }({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337121/field-1" "q-337121/field-2" "q-337121/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337121"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228342 :answer-field/correct 17592186228345 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186229652 :question/answer-fields 17592186228333] {:db/id "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/86cc1658e625ae810e72e8acf1042be3e1f61749b982ae7ff104797635ee0737" :answer/id #uuid "4bce935a-ef9c-503f-865b-700800ca1757" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using the fact that ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" :answer/id #uuid "3fbea789-b450-5264-9cbf-abd3fc42ff3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/e3a6cb9e213c821a3331fe56ca04bc11dcb8155e9f4846775e85149d35b3cb76" :answer/id #uuid "a4a3743a-0336-55d5-b424-3b88edb16cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "by substitution from line $\\text{L2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2216ce1-702a-57ab-b1d9-ab74958872fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/86cc1658e625ae810e72e8acf1042be3e1f61749b982ae7ff104797635ee0737" "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/2a4d337181ecb06ec78d833aec5a2a0d437a10731b9adf12e8bd7517cb3a4cb1" "q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7/e3a6cb9e213c821a3331fe56ca04bc11dcb8155e9f4846775e85149d35b3cb76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186229652 :question/answer-fields 17592186228337] {:db/id "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/3030c4b4faeb21331eace8593f31cb2c1a36ea5deda837717e9af04acea6148d" :answer/id #uuid "cec58bca-e058-5b38-8126-ad2515c389e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bt-B{t}_{0}=B(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/c9c71b8ca55d1137be67edf118c4ee642a57d3bd36b599c1f365b783422f43fc" :answer/id #uuid "d0b0afce-6fdd-5b29-8e3e-2c93a8e6856f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{Mt}{e}^{-M{t}_{0}}={e}^{M(t-{t}_{0})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/bdcc209ada28288d6eb8133014ef9a8b516df1c1e43b86db917cf5179ff24132" :answer/id #uuid "4c787050-5597-56bf-a9dd-3e310cbf9f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At}$ for any matrix $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595" :answer/id #uuid "a93e4dab-4047-5b15-ac8e-c9060a1b01f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691" :answer-field/id #uuid "da577183-f523-5e31-9052-33db386794ad" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595" :answer-field/choices ["q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/3030c4b4faeb21331eace8593f31cb2c1a36ea5deda837717e9af04acea6148d" "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/c9c71b8ca55d1137be67edf118c4ee642a57d3bd36b599c1f365b783422f43fc" "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/bdcc209ada28288d6eb8133014ef9a8b516df1c1e43b86db917cf5179ff24132" "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691/4f5bbf4e07cc492a1d173bf17d1940aa912a5dd83524d301b2c7602c6e6ea595"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-336639"] :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ is true by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ is true by $\\text{the properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336639/field-2/ma-v1/65659b26c767ca002a92e6e7dd3e297b13ced54f2409e31f51db5487a90745c7" "q-336639/field-3/ma-v1/3762ffc1cd82a94229fa79d7623aac8fbd2cb03a02673b15cd5c012770374691"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-1/f9a19a1e4ef25fbe358c30392fb376b23bcdec3b9f44cd0a3c8cd608faebde58" :answer/id #uuid "dcaece5d-98eb-5ff5-8dd0-8001e05689c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-1/ff45d543689998885a74e01906015e6cb6cef20473028322dec2380ac2337128" :answer/id #uuid "356ef949-654a-564c-8624-fc0a40a8c4da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-1/366ee9d9cdb8fd8597d50c6049dd1c5ab181f3ec88c7152fbc9bd88fe473b825" :answer/id #uuid "d22e282d-e968-57bd-a400-9b46374a3b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-1/527639d10d4434985d0dd58bbe391e1c198194b63f1087b0aeead6f6bc5d11af" :answer/id #uuid "af3238f3-8dad-51e6-a839-59c6b1b35639" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c23d50a-e0c5-571b-9eb3-58edcba636a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336477/field-1/366ee9d9cdb8fd8597d50c6049dd1c5ab181f3ec88c7152fbc9bd88fe473b825" :answer-field/choices ["q-336477/field-1/f9a19a1e4ef25fbe358c30392fb376b23bcdec3b9f44cd0a3c8cd608faebde58" "q-336477/field-1/ff45d543689998885a74e01906015e6cb6cef20473028322dec2380ac2337128" "q-336477/field-1/366ee9d9cdb8fd8597d50c6049dd1c5ab181f3ec88c7152fbc9bd88fe473b825" "q-336477/field-1/527639d10d4434985d0dd58bbe391e1c198194b63f1087b0aeead6f6bc5d11af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-2/527639d10d4434985d0dd58bbe391e1c198194b63f1087b0aeead6f6bc5d11af" :answer/id #uuid "b4291bd1-0f84-522a-b3fd-0b40c2f29760" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-2/ff45d543689998885a74e01906015e6cb6cef20473028322dec2380ac2337128" :answer/id #uuid "c82b79b0-2020-523b-b78f-7b9a63fdbc80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-2/4909495bf9091f30373cbd5c855b6c3764e80ddba9421c961ad21c8f01f7a355" :answer/id #uuid "f69a3de3-c983-54ae-bee2-c4c8ba371278" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-2/366ee9d9cdb8fd8597d50c6049dd1c5ab181f3ec88c7152fbc9bd88fe473b825" :answer/id #uuid "a224a950-6e6d-5bdb-89f8-51806ec8e0b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ba404e-73f7-5d6b-81b1-2958204552dd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336477/field-2/4909495bf9091f30373cbd5c855b6c3764e80ddba9421c961ad21c8f01f7a355" :answer-field/choices ["q-336477/field-2/527639d10d4434985d0dd58bbe391e1c198194b63f1087b0aeead6f6bc5d11af" "q-336477/field-2/ff45d543689998885a74e01906015e6cb6cef20473028322dec2380ac2337128" "q-336477/field-2/4909495bf9091f30373cbd5c855b6c3764e80ddba9421c961ad21c8f01f7a355" "q-336477/field-2/366ee9d9cdb8fd8597d50c6049dd1c5ab181f3ec88c7152fbc9bd88fe473b825"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" :answer/id #uuid "fd813941-3036-583d-9df8-56a68146e586" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-3/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3" :answer/id #uuid "557c4f89-4242-5f97-8005-e6446b47851a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-3/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004" :answer/id #uuid "bf8cc8cd-5d63-5bea-9bbc-226b8cb68088" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-3/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018" :answer/id #uuid "8e37e049-d868-5f49-8ec5-9efe2cabc43f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc25b498-2f29-5f2d-accc-61ff65ef3717" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336477/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" :answer-field/choices ["q-336477/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" "q-336477/field-3/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3" "q-336477/field-3/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004" "q-336477/field-3/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477" :question/id #uuid "b476f440-04ac-55c0-bbfe-8012f8f71f27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336477" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from $\\text{L2},$ we have the identity\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336477/field-1" "q-336477/field-2" "q-336477/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-1/175c061f136a442ead0b94a6c0974d0f9f0863371621fd38a66dce770c7a4278" :answer/id #uuid "ffe28982-653c-5939-835d-a2ccb30c9411" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-1/ec492fb997e3afd0d7bc3be56c2489fbe121747f459e8478e0349a3fa01939e8" :answer/id #uuid "73c194e4-916d-56d7-842a-bfffc2649a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A{t}_{0}}I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-1/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02" :answer/id #uuid "32600af2-86f3-5c68-b6cf-19eb20e20f69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31719cee-0dd9-5e45-813d-1bb46b0079d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337115/field-1/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02" :answer-field/choices ["q-337115/field-1/175c061f136a442ead0b94a6c0974d0f9f0863371621fd38a66dce770c7a4278" "q-337115/field-1/ec492fb997e3afd0d7bc3be56c2489fbe121747f459e8478e0349a3fa01939e8" "q-337115/field-1/79e53f8b6d577cf6087caa8d369ecc11ff39de1dbe34717a3d8d40f0fe957d02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-2/3aa6f3d85394d9e48304ff8e0ca20dc68533c9cc8fabc9853fd3423b253f219a" :answer/id #uuid "6a3b167a-3a1e-5a33-9ee4-ab2f9073af79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-2/fd852797230cb4bc761a96249fee0497b5e88847d02d142ecc023787fb17f696" :answer/id #uuid "816df69c-d0c7-5f1c-93ff-722c59d6ebce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t=0$ and solving for $c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b" :answer/id #uuid "33a97701-9497-5973-bc9a-5ee9d3160762" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e49f41-3cbb-58eb-b430-fb0279c56075" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337115/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b" :answer-field/choices ["q-337115/field-2/3aa6f3d85394d9e48304ff8e0ca20dc68533c9cc8fabc9853fd3423b253f219a" "q-337115/field-2/fd852797230cb4bc761a96249fee0497b5e88847d02d142ecc023787fb17f696" "q-337115/field-2/ed95b64e164fb40772d373ca50874f6d79b77c64bf52980113ace7d2a414842b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-3/599639b5df3ebf712fd16c50ab025f19e06ba3cd548544d0dd4e75edfeec16c6" :answer/id #uuid "7275b08a-542e-593d-8443-bffbe10cdf92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{X+Y}={e}^{X}{e}^{Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-3/0ab695b1b00723214357482793b570b757b454d95d8d683d45d3f161216563d5" :answer/id #uuid "6780975d-ce21-542b-897b-cfc796887506" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-3/b3843477e8a895979106908f837ede3486c37f64e0f1a0d97f97b0b4c2f43b7f" :answer/id #uuid "5aa7637f-c9a0-50ab-a0ec-e57dffa55bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A({t}_{0}-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f2a8e74-8c53-5a91-aff3-1d0ac19bea0e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337115/field-3/0ab695b1b00723214357482793b570b757b454d95d8d683d45d3f161216563d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-337115/field-3/599639b5df3ebf712fd16c50ab025f19e06ba3cd548544d0dd4e75edfeec16c6" "q-337115/field-3/0ab695b1b00723214357482793b570b757b454d95d8d683d45d3f161216563d5" "q-337115/field-3/b3843477e8a895979106908f837ede3486c37f64e0f1a0d97f97b0b4c2f43b7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337115" :question/id #uuid "fb80bbdf-275a-5f01-a2dc-fafc9f40d1ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-337115" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L8}$ and $\\text{L9}.$ Starting from $\\text{L8},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ to get\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L9}.$ Thus, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }{t}_{0}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337115/field-1" "q-337115/field-2" "q-337115/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21707"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to the system of ODEs above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/5388e1d5a2d29c3930b904d418b3a69615683bff1278d45a202d8405b150cede.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/85fc07cc4bce6e748a6b0184a3fc0a1ef75bf37e29d68ea45cbbb94892d5b58d.png)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/7f047425e15df4bb6bd8284f0e6267227ba31f6a251ceb45e040e6a508b519d6.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/2dff913b6a0163c9dff6e28d81690472f043de69e4796dffb58b16b933165450.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/c31b507ed2dac736cf47cbee9a967be4f4dc7deda44776e27a62be953834905b.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/716aafac0120d14538c3cb2cea689450e9655f0d94147b04c0903c3bb5cde753.png)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} & t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21725"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/ddc88d8b24bc6bc4ea37107bc2419d3e3bd2607c1135531c01ce9ae85bc2b5c7.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/5ad7137465faba80d0da35cf68c609af07cd3241740a6f7e2163a6dd0653884b.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/fddbe93ca2141bf2590d292fb0d2b3ca9520bb33c531ee03d9431b92617da3e2.png)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/e1ea5cd8cc5f4a5fdacc8978c37f9a4fee7a7e05c688c9e80a30f7503c6faae3.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/37f073b62d4f7475211494e2c90f5ea9f806328dbbff3647b869615aba0110c4.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/9f1fef4580872d201662d38ce4f2babe02ef1ac782953eac2ec951c426d49174.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{x}(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/dad0a2186f78aae6569b2d880e29a570f44b289a2fd1d804e989a3356b7f0074.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21723"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/c9fe7104001d89b4266ab760530a1db5abee0cb9206a53d374827892db114296.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/bf7bc97a737f653b03369fa91a29f564703abf6172aba7ba6db62acae12c1af4.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/d63e1f20fcf33dd0ba20d1ba2be8ae008888e794c0054da8b8628f182c501068.png)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/cdd98c904dce4f0beebc1333ce00f3f54551a93eddb5a8e52af6392946c2f910.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/2dff913b6a0163c9dff6e28d81690472f043de69e4796dffb58b16b933165450.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/b6e79ba4308d37fec08efa34e15e009e938fc6df4bceba677837897c21602397.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\mathbf{c} =e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t = t_0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nand since $e^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21711"] :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\qquad \\Phi_0(0) = I_n.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,\\mathbf{c}$ for some constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At}\\,\\mathbf{c}$ \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $(e^{A t_0})^{-1} \\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1} e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{c} = e^{-A t_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} e^{-At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At - At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{A(t-t_0)} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\nFill in the blanks to justify each step of the following reasoning.\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/49f634e53afe213a0c192e6ef60e8499801a86a8d6a87d1776fafa62cef3192f.png)\n\n$\\qquad$ The property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/8b875a680318b797dc6b78d1c73b0012ede83a412435efafaf3064321fc406ee.png)\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/e576e779eada3b3a299cf45e14a1d6fbdfca5aa852bf2eb7eea70bdb22e0f41d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L4}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L4},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $(e^{At_0})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n(e^{A t_0})^{-1}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1}e^{A t_0}\\,\\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/22142a26bf70dc1ee58e7d7643acdad468ddfd7c9dc48c816f136afcae4d1320.png)\n\n- Next, we justify the step $\\textrm{L7}$ to $\\textrm{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-At_0$ commute, we may combine exponentials:\n\n$$\ne^{At}e^{-At_0}=e^{At-At_0}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\textrm{L7}$ produces line $\\textrm{L8}.$ Hence, the property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/bab6ad7c1621beb36d016e72f1e040206b9bf70a2e21ff266ba5b71495a23ae2.png)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L8}$ and $\\textrm{L9}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L8},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At-At_0}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-At_0=A(t-t_0)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L9}.$ Thus, $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt lightgray]{At-At_0=A(t-t_0)\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }t_0}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
